@theme family
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
hint: Has the Mail come yet? It hasn't, has it. I'll check again.
mem: mail
them: I keep checking my Mail. Don't mind me. Nothing's wrong. I'm just checking.
them: Relay's slow this week. Everybody's waiting on something.
? choice
* Waiting on anything good?   flavour:listen mem:asked
  them: Just news. From home. The ordinary kind, I hope.
* The relay's always slow. Says so in the manual.   flavour:cheer
  them: Does it? Page one, probably. "This will be slow." I believe it.   [laugh]
them: Right. I'll check again in an hour. Or ten minutes.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
needs: family
hint: Sit with me a bit? I don't want to talk about it. I want to talk about it.
mem: worry
them: It's {family}. Not well. They've gone into hospital, back home. For tests.   [sigh]
them: They say it's probably nothing. "Probably" is a big word from this far away.
them: I can't do anything from here. I can't even sit with them.
? choice
* I'm here. You can sit with me instead, for now.   flavour:listen mem:sat
  them: Yeah. Thanks. That's something. That's a lot, actually.
  + them: Thanks. I'll take that. Just sit. You don't have to say anything. That's the best bit.
* Ask the Comms lot to tell you the moment news comes in.   flavour:practical mem:comms
  them: Can I? I'll ask. Then at least I won't have to keep checking.
* When my family was worried about me, letters helped. Write one?   flavour:share mem:letter
  them: A letter. Yes. Something they can hold. I'll write tonight.
them: Thanks for sitting. I'll be all right. I'm all right now, actually. For now.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
needs: family
hint: News came. Come here. I want to tell someone, and I want it to be you.
mem: news
them: News came this morning. {family}'s home. Tired, still a bit poorly, but home.
them: They read my letter in the hospital. Twice, they said. It was a terrible letter.   [laugh]
them: I was so far away. And it was all right anyway. I didn't know that could happen.
? choice
* I'm so glad.   flavour:listen
  them: Me too. More than I can say. So I won't. I'll just say thanks.
  + them: Me too. You were there for the worst bit. I won't forget that. Not ever.
* Celebrate? Pudding's on me.   flavour:cheer mem:pudding
  them: Pudding. Yes. Two puddings. It's that kind of day.   [laugh]
them: I'm going to call home tonight. Just to hear them be ordinary.
